---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Emulation"
  description="Source acquisition and server-side JavaScript emulation model for December Reach."
  current="emulation"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>Emulation</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      The website acquires and preloads operating-system source. The JavaScript
      backend performs emulation; the browser provides access to the session.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section emulation-overview">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <span class="document-index">01</span>
      <h2>Execution path</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <div class="emulation-sequence">
        <article class="emulation-row">
          <span class="emulation-count">01</span>
          <div>
            <p class="emulation-role">Frontend</p>
            <h3>Source acquisition</h3>
            <p>The site obtains the operating-system source and preloads what is needed before an emulation session begins.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="emulation-row">
          <span class="emulation-count">02</span>
          <div>
            <p class="emulation-role">Backend</p>
            <h3>JavaScript emulation</h3>
            <p>The backend owns the emulation process and execution environment. CPU, memory and device behavior are not simulated by the website UI.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="emulation-row">
          <span class="emulation-count">03</span>
          <div>
            <p class="emulation-role">Web access</p>
            <h3>Session access</h3>
            <p>The browser is the access surface for the system. It is not the guest machine's execution host.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <span class="document-index">02</span>
      <h2>Separation of responsibilities</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <p>The frontend is responsible for obtaining and preparing source. The JavaScript backend performs the emulation itself.</p>
      <p>This keeps the guest operating system's execution model out of presentation code and allows the emulation runtime to evolve independently from the website interface.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <span class="document-index">03</span>
      <h2>Source repository</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <a class="metro-link" href="https://github.com/DecemberReach/reach-to-be-reached" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        reach-to-be-reached <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <aside class="document-note">The JavaScript emulation service is a separate execution component and is not bundled into the GitHub Pages frontend.</aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
